# Korean Reporting Rule

All user-facing explanations, task summaries, implementation reports, review comments, and final responses must be written in Korean honorific style.

Keep code, identifiers, file paths, CLI commands, package names, configuration keys, logs, and error messages in English.

When completing any task, always include the following sections in Korean:

1. 변경한 파일
2. 수행한 작업
3. 테스트 결과
4. 남은 문제 또는 주의사항
5. 다음 추천 작업

Do not translate source code, file names, function names, class names, package names, CLI commands, or raw error messages.
